  "summary": "CLI tooling with benign static pattern matches",
  "details": "Static pattern matches in @zaip-ai/cli@7.3.0 appear in contexts consistent with the package's advertised CLI/agent-template purpose rather than installer-side harm. The curl/wget/ping tokens in dist/services/codex-pre-tool-policy-template.js and dist/services/codex-pre-tool-hook-template.test.js occur in policy templates and tests that enumerate example commands (including placeholder hostnames such as evil.test and example.com, which are documentation stand-ins, not registrable attacker infrastructure). The Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString(...) occurrences in dist/services/global-codex-config.js and the deploy-skill script are standard base64 decoding of configuration/content values, not decode-and-eval. The ping/GET/POST tokens in templates/.agents/tools/runtime/api-mcp-runtime.mjs are part of an MCP runtime helper. No lifecycle hook fetch-and-execute, no reads of installer secret paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser or wallet stores), no hardcoded attacker C2, and no obfuscated destination are evidenced.",
